      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict confirmed_exact: position confirmed at this residue. validation_level surface_only -> function_only (paper reports surface: no, function: yes). Paper (PMID 19721821): \"converting the sequence DKEAPTGS (residues 94-101) in the exon E2 region of PTH1R to DYKDDDDK of Flag epitope\". Audit note: Human PTH1R (593 aa, Gardella template); DKEAPTGS = canonical 94-101, so junction after E93 is right, but this is an 8-residue REPLACEMENT not an insertion. Surface display never shown (anti-Flag immunoblot of NP-40 lysates only); function shown (PTH-stimulated cAMP and ERK1/2 like WT). validation_level surface_only is wrong: function without surface. Read via PMC page by WebFetch (PMC full text API returned empty).] L1 names residues 94\u2013101 (DKEAPTGS) as the replaced block; Python confirmed seq[93:101]='DKEAPTGS' exactly. The junction is insert_after_residue=93 (seq[92]='E'), with residue_after=seq[93]='D' (first residue of the replaced block). Position 93\u2013101 lies deep within the large N-terminal ECD (landmarks: extracellular 27\u2013186), 86 residues from TM1, well clear of any TM boundary. The nearest ECD cysteines are at positions 108 and 117, both outside the replaced block. Full-length human PTH1R construct in which residues 94\u2013101 (DKEAPTGS, exon E2 region) were replaced by the FLAG sequence (DYKDDDDK) by PCR overlap extension; the tagged receptor was used to detect surface-expressed PTH1R in the absence of a commercial antibody.",
      "residue_after": "D",
      "residue_before": "E",
      "residue_label": "E93",
      "residue_range": null,
      "site_id": "PTH1R-internal-93-lit",
      "site_kind": "internal",
      "source_tier": "paper",
      "sources": [
        {
          "pmid": 19721821,
          "citation": "PMID 19721821",
          "claim": "Parathyroid hormone (PTH) regulates bone remodeling and calcium and phosphate homeostasis. PTH actions are mediated by type I PTH/PTH-related peptide receptor (PTH1R). There has been no commercially available, specific antibody to detect human PTH1R expression so far. Flag-tagged human PTH1R construct, converting the sequence DKEAPTGS (residues 94-101) in the exon E2 region of PTH1R to DYKDDDDK of Flag epitope, was generated by using PCR overlap extension or ligase enzyme for two-fragment assembly.",
          "title": "Generation of human PTH1R construct with FLAG epitope located internally: comparison of two-fragment assembly by using PCR overlap extension or ligase",
