      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "L4/L5/L6 explicitly state HiBiT is fused to the N-terminus of full-length PTH1R; the signal peptide spans residues 1\u201326 (landmarks), so the mature N-terminus is residue 27 and the tag sits at the 26/27 junction. Python confirmed seq[25]='V' and seq[26]='D'. This is the only extracellular terminus of PTH1R (C-terminus is intracellular, residues 463\u2013593), making the junction unambiguous. L2 and L3 provide independent corroboration of the same junction with FLAG and HA tags respectively. Full-length PTH1R with HiBiT fused to its N-terminus (HiBiT-PTH1R) expressed in HEK293 cells; the tag is placed after the signal peptide cleavage site (mature N-terminus = residue 27), confirmed at the plasma membrane by LgBiT/substrate luminescence under non-permeabilized conditions. L2 (PMC12643933) independently places a FLAG tag at the identical junction ('between the HA signal sequence and PTH1R coding sequence'), and L3 (PMC8682804) reports stable MDCK cell lines expressing HA-tagged PTH1R at the cell surface.",
